{
  "_notes": [
    "Spider-Man Vault Edition V1.00 (smanve_100). Until this map index.json pointed smanve_100 at",
    "smanve_101.map.json, but V1.00 is the offset-0 adjustment layout and V1.01 the +2 one, its",
    "champion records sit 0x10 lower and its CPU counters elsewhere: through that map a Free Play",
    "or Balls Per Game write landed on another adjustment and every champion read straddled two records.",
    "Derived from smanve_101.map.json by moving each address to where the smanve_100 ROM keeps it",
    "(backport tools/samrom/samrom.py): Free Play record 33 (ROM adjustment ID 34) 0x02102110, Balls",
    "Per Game 0x021020F8, Credit Limit 0x02102108; GC, HS1-HS4 and the seven mode champions from",
    "0x02102B70 in 32-byte records (checksum16 at +28). Scores (0x021109E4, 4 apart), credits, player",
    "count and Master Volume (0x02110250) are where V1.01 keeps them. Mode champions as on smanve_101:",
    "Combo and Spider hold counts, Best Combo a one-byte count at +0x1A.",
    "A headless libpinmame run of smanve_100 (two players, two tilts, factory NVRAM) validates every",
    "record by its checksum, the three adjustments and Master Volume (40, check byte 215) by their",
    "check bytes. Player and ball are at 0x000325B4/0x000325B5 (the ROM's only candidate outside the",
    "round addresses that have never been real), the status byte at 0x000325E6 = player + 0x32:",
    "01 in attract, 13 in play, 15 from each tilt to the next ball, as on sman_261. game_over is any",
    "bit above 0x01 (mask 0xFE inverted); tilted is an enum over mask 0x1F with only 21 (0x15) true."
  ],
